    "body": "- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\nHey, big fan. I noticed that sometimes I want to jump to something, then realize I wanted to jump to something else. Stopping the jump on cursor move works, but I happen to have muscle memory to mash escape whenever I want to \"cancel\" something. This PR adds a simple on_key listener for escape to stop jumping in a similar vein to the on_cursormoved callback",
    "closed_at": "2025-05-17T10:48:06Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the PR!\r\n\r\nThis is already possible with custom mapping:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal jump_stop = function()\r\n  if not MiniJump.state.jumping then return '<Esc>' end\r\n  MiniJump.stop_jumping()\r\nend\r\nvim.keymap.set({ 'n', 'x', 'o' }, '<Esc>', jump_stop, { expr = true, desc = 'Stop jumping' })\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt might be a good idea to have something like this built-in or documented as an example. I'll need to think about it.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nIn the future, please follow the 'CONTRIBUTING.md' and create an issue first before making a PR. This usually saves time for both parties.",
